This commit introduces the vulnerable construct in `pidff_init_fields`. Specifically, it replaces the sequential `clear_bit` calls with a short-circuiting logical OR (`||`) chain of `test_and_clear_bit` calls:

c
	if (PIDFF_FIND_FIELDS(set_condition, PID_SET_CONDITION, 1)) {
		if (test_and_clear_bit(FF_SPRING, dev->ffbit)   ||
		    test_and_clear_bit(FF_DAMPER, dev->ffbit)   ||
		    test_and_clear_bit(FF_FRICTION, dev->ffbit) ||
		    test_and_clear_bit(FF_INERTIA, dev->ffbit))
			hid_warn(pidff->hid, "unknown condition effect layout\n");
	}


If `test_and_clear_bit(FF_SPRING, ...)` evaluates to true, the remaining `test_and_clear_bit` calls for `FF_DAMPER`, `FF_FRICTION`, and `FF_INERTIA` are skipped due to short-circuiting, leaving those bits uncleared in `dev->ffbit`.
